## Hints for Future Agents
- _checkpoints_to_rotate is pure and takes (full_path, basename) pairs where full_path is a local path
  OR a canonical msc:// URI; storage.list_checkpoint_dirs returns strings for both backends now, so the
  helper is backend-agnostic. The iter_NNNNNNN regex filter runs on basename, so non-iter dirs
  (e.g. "not_a_checkpoint") are never rotated.
- _restore_fp32_master_params checks storage.exists(optim_dir) AND storage.exists(join(optim_dir,
  ".metadata")); the .metadata probe works for both backends (verified via the remote DCP round-trip).
- train_config._ALWAYS_LOCAL_PATH_KEYS = ("output_dir","cache_dir","model_download_dir"); adding
  checkpoint_dir there would break msc:// URIs by absolutizing them. Do NOT add it.

